}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the recording-channel mechanism: specify where coverage[\"overlap\"][\"status\"] is written on the NORMAL review path (run_pass1 mutating the coverage dict seeded at production_batch_runner.py:134 and returned as batch_plan at :197), since the cited coverage_extra/indeterminate_verdict seam (claimability.py:132/153) fires only on the early INDETERMINATE returns at __init__.py:383/:392.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'The status is recorded under coverage[\"overlap\"] via the coverage_extra seam, which src/rebar/llm/plan_review/claimability.py:132 accepts then :153 merges into coverage ... the mechanism :120 uses for not_claimable.'","claimability.py:127-153: coverage_extra is a parameter of indeterminate_verdict only; its sole callers are the not-claimable fast-fail (claimability.py:120) and the two early returns in __init__.py:383 (not-claimable) and :392 (plan_relation_snapshot_error).","On the normal path the LLM runs, so none of these early returns fire; coverage is seeded in ProductionBatchRunner.run (production_batch_runner.py:134) and returned as outputs['batch_plan'] at :197 after run_pass1 mutates it in place -- coverage_extra/indeterminate_verdict is never invoked there.","The overlap ACs ('When the index is absent, coverage[\"overlap\"][\"status\"] is index-absent', etc.) assert the record on the normal review path, but the cited mechanism only runs on paths where no overlap retrieval or LLM finder executes."],"finding":"The plan's recording-channel mechanism is miscited: the coverage_extra seam at claimability.py:132/153 is the indeterminate_verdict parameter used ONLY on early INDETERMINATE returns, not on the normal LLM review path where an overlap finding is produced.","group_criteria":["E4","G6"],"group_id":"g9c3a42c4ca6407f8","id":"f95751b133ffcef79","impact":1.0,"is_primary":true,"location":"Approach → 'Recording channel: the existing coverage merge'; ACs for coverage[\"overlap\"][\"status\"]","norm_id":"n8a12dedcc12ad753","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["overlap=True review with absent index / failed catch-up / provider-error: the normal path runs, but the plan's named coverage_extra seam is never reached, so coverage[\"overlap\"] is not written by the cited mechanism."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Record the overlap status by having the overlap module / run_pass1 write coverage[\"overlap\"] directly into the coverage dict that ProductionBatchRunner.run seeds and run_pass1 fills in place; thread coverage into _chunk_extra_context (or its new overlap call) rather than routing through indeterminate_verdict's coverage_extra parameter.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate the full `overlap` threading edit-set outside the plan_review dir: add the `overlap` parameter to `gate_dispatch.produce_plan_review_verdict` and its run_workflow input dict, declare `overlap` under `inputs:` in `gates/plan-review.yaml` and wire `${{ inputs.overlap }}` into the finders batch `with:`, and pass `overlap` from `review_plan` through to `produce_plan_review_verdict`.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["gate_dispatch.py:71 `produce_plan_review_verdict(..., probe_criteria=None, ...)`","gate_dispatch.py:183 injects `\"probe_criteria\": list(probe_criteria or [])` into the run_workflow input dict","gates/plan-review.yaml:24-30 declares `probe_criteria` under `inputs:`; :54 and :66 wire `${{ inputs.probe_criteria }}` into the assemble and finders-batch `with:`","production_batch_runner.py:123 reads `req.with_inputs.get(\"probe_criteria\")`","review_plan (__init__.py:473) reaches the batch only via gate_dispatch.produce_plan_review_verdict, never building BatchRunRequest directly — `BatchRunRequest` has no match under src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","The plan's edit-set only names pass1.py, overlap.py (new), similar/__init__.py, claimability.py, and 'where the batch request is assembled' without identifying that site"],"finding":"The `overlap` parameter's path to `req.with_inputs` omits the workflow-plumbing edit targets. The cited precedent `probe_criteria` is not set by a single assignment: it is threaded review_plan -> gate_dispatch.produce_plan_review_verdict (parameter) -> the run_workflow input dict -> the gates/plan-review.yaml `inputs:` block -> the batch step `with:` (${{ inputs.probe_criteria }}) -> ProductionBatchRunner.run req.with_inputs. For `overlap` to arrive at req.with_inputs the same layers must be edited, and the plan names none of them.","group_criteria":["G1G2","G6"],"group_id":"gda643cfba1b4b0a1","id":"f692a05a94f25cc3e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":true,"location":"Approach, 'On demand, not on every review.' paragraph ('overlap rides req.with_inputs ... set where the batch request is assembled, read in ProductionBatchRunner.run')","norm_id":"nae5f2b013bef3c8d","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer sets overlap in review_plan but it never reaches ProductionBatchRunner because the YAML input and batch `with:` were not updated","overlap stays silently default-off in production because the workflow input is undeclared"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Replace 'set where the batch request is assembled, read in ProductionBatchRunner.run' with an explicit chain naming gate_dispatch.produce_plan_review_verdict (new param + input-dict key), gates/plan-review.yaml (new `inputs.overlap` + batch `with: overlap: ${{ inputs.overlap }}`), and the review_plan->produce_plan_review_verdict pass-through, mirroring how probe_criteria is threaded.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the recording channel: state that coverage['overlap'] is written directly into the run-scoped coverage dict seeded in ProductionBatchRunner.run (threaded through run_pass1 / overlap.py), since the coverage_extra->indeterminate_verdict seam fires only on non-LLM early-return INDETERMINATE verdicts, not on the overlap review path.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'The status is recorded under coverage[\"overlap\"] via the coverage_extra seam, which src/rebar/llm/plan_review/claimability.py:132 accepts then :153 merges into coverage'","claimability.indeterminate_verdict merges coverage_extra only inside the INDETERMINATE early-return builder (claimability.py:136-153)","All four coverage_extra call sites are early-return/INDETERMINATE builders: plan_relation_snapshot_error (__init__.py:392), retry_refused (retry.py:168), not_claimable (claimability.py:120), cancelled (plan_review_recovery.py:430)","A normal overlap=True review runs run_pass1 and returns coverage verbatim as outputs['batch_plan']=coverage (production_batch_runner.py:134,197) — it never calls indeterminate_verdict, so the coverage_extra seam is not on that path"],"finding":"The named recording channel (coverage_extra -> claimability.indeterminate_verdict -> coverage) is unreachable on the path that produces overlap findings; it serves only the non-LLM early-return INDETERMINATE verdicts.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":"g9c3a42c4ca6407f8","id":"fe7181f847b90d49b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":false,"location":"Approach / 'Recording channel: the existing coverage merge'","norm_id":"n8bdbcb4bd1127ed7","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["overlap=True on a plan that reaches a PASS or BLOCK verdict (LLM ran) — the status would need to appear in coverage['overlap'] but the named seam never executes"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Record the diagnostic by assigning coverage['overlap'] = {'status': ..., 'detail': ...} on the coverage dict that ProductionBatchRunner.run passes into run_pass1 (which is emitted verbatim as batch_plan), rather than via claimability's coverage_extra.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Re-ground the overlap threading on the real seam: review_plan -> _run_plan_review -> gate workflow (gates/plan-review.yaml with:) -> interpreter resolved_with -> req.with_inputs['overlap'] -> ProductionBatchRunner.run, matching how probe_criteria is actually threaded (gate_dispatch.py + plan-review.yaml), rather than claiming review_plan builds a BatchRunRequest at production_batch_runner.py:152.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'review_plan does not call run_pass1: its only src/ caller is ProductionBatchRunner.run, which builds the call at production_batch_runner.py:152 from a BatchRunRequest'","production_batch_runner.py:152 is the run_pass1(...) call, not a call to review_plan","review_plan runs through the v3 engine workflow gates/plan-review.yaml via _run_plan_review (__init__.py:239 'Verdict production runs through the v3 engine workflow', :265 _run_plan_review) — it does not construct a BatchRunRequest","with_inputs is set by the workflow interpreter: interpreter.py:397 with_inputs=resolved_with; probe_criteria reaches req.with_inputs via gate YAML with: (plan-review.yaml:54,66) + gate_dispatch.py:183 + the interpreter, not via review_plan"],"finding":"The overlap-parameter threading is anchored to a non-existent seam: review_plan does not build a BatchRunRequest; it runs the gate workflow YAML, and with_inputs is populated by the interpreter, so the path from overlap=True to req.with_inputs['overlap'] is undescribed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":"gda643cfba1b4b0a1","id":"f39a6589f01ee3273","impact":1.0,"is_primary":false,"location":"Approach / 'On demand, not on every review'","norm_id":"ne0ea5cfa53d7dbbc","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementing overlap:bool on review_plan and expecting it to appear as req.with_inputs['overlap'] without touching the gate YAML / gate_dispatch / interpreter resolved_with layer"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the decision-rule/instruction text co-located with the injected overlap candidates (mirroring decomposition_state_block) that directs the Pass-1 finder to judge overlap against the plan and emit one advisory finding naming each overlapping candidate.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Both existing extra_context blocks carry an explicit protocol co-located with the facts: decomposition_state_block (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_lint.py:58-62) says 'do NOT count children yourself, and do NOT flag this ticket as flat... Judge only the QUALITY'; _no_file_impact_context (pass1.py:161) labels its payload '## Declared no-file-impact context'","passes.py:231-235: extra_context is 'authoritative, store-derived context prepended to the rubric instructions' — the finder acts on it only via the instructions it carries","The plan says overlap.py 'builds the candidate text' and '_chunk_extra_context gains only the call' but never states the judging/emit instruction that must accompany the candidate list"],"finding":"The plan specifies injecting overlap candidates into the Pass-1 extra_context and states 'the existing Pass-1 unit does the judging' and emits an advisory overlap finding, but never specifies the instruction/decision-rule text co-located with those candidates that tells the finder to judge overlap and emit an advisory finding naming the candidate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdd349067e1b0911a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Ride the existing Pass-1 extra-context seam' and 'Findings are advisory'","norm_id":"n919612e04424c470","priority":0.65,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A Pass-1 finder receives a list of candidate tickets with no co-located rule and does not know to compare them against the plan or to emit a finding at all"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In overlap.py's context builder, emit a labelled block (e.g. '## OVERLAP CANDIDATES (from similar-ticket index)') followed by an explicit rule: for each candidate whose plan this plan restates, emit ONE advisory finding naming that candidate id and why it overlaps; never block; a child/follow-up/deliberate split is not an overlap.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.65,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the criterion id that gates overlap-candidate injection in _chunk_extra_context and that the emitted advisory overlap finding carries in criteria[], or state explicitly how the finding is routed without a criterion.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2645,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Search of src/rebar/llm/criteria for 'overlap' returns no matches — no overlap criterio